  "question": {
    "text": "The system shown in the figure is in equilibrium and all the blocks are at rest. Assume that the masses of the strings, the pulley and the spring are negligible with respect to the masses of the blocks and friction is absent. Find the acceleration of block <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, just after cutting the string <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>. [<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>]<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"assets\\qt0009_1a61f50f58b7.jpeg\" />"
